course: dictionary
lesson: 1945
title: Committee: a chosen group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A committee is a small group of people chosen to make decisions or plan something for a bigger group. The word names the people, not the job. «The eco committee met on Monday to plan the school garden.» The committee makes the plans, and the whole school gets to enjoy the garden.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Chosen tells you the members were picked, so not everyone is in it. Decisions and plan tell you what the group does. Try the check: swap in "a small group chosen to plan" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Committees are found in many places: in schools, clubs, churches and governments. In a sentence about making a law, «a committee that checks it line by line» means a small group reads the plan very carefully before everyone votes on it.
fact: A committee is a group of people chosen to make decisions or plan something for a bigger group.
fact: «Committee» is a noun, and its plural is committees.
fact: A committee meeting is when the members come together to talk and decide.
fact: To be on a committee means you are one of its members.
fact: In law-making, a committee may check a bill line by line before it is voted on.
exercise: What is a committee? | *A small group chosen to make decisions or plan something for a bigger group | A loud argument between friends | A single person who makes all the rules alone | A type of school dinner
exercise: «The eco committee met on Monday to plan the school garden.» Find one word that tells you the committee makes plans. | met | Monday | garden | *plan
exercise: What is a committee meeting? | A quiet lunch break in the library | *When committee members come together to talk and decide | A race around the playing field | When the whole school sings a song together
test: «A bill goes through readings, a committee that checks it line by line, and changes before it becomes law.» What does committee mean here? | A single judge in a court | *A small group chosen to check the bill carefully | A group made up of every citizen in the country | A type of document
test: Which is the plural of committee? | committeed | committys | *committees | committee's
exam: Mum says, «I've been asked to sit on the school committee.» What does sit on a committee mean? | *To be one of its members | To lie down and rest | To sit on a hard chair during the meeting | To be the head teacher of the school
